# P-006 — CONNECTOR UNIFICATION LAYER

## (GitHub + Supabase + MCP Orchestration Backbone)

### Purpose

Create a single abstraction layer that removes direct tool fragmentation and enforces **one routing surface for all external writes/reads**:

* GitHub (code + commits + repo state)
* Supabase (memory, events, audit, execution traces)
* MCP (tool registry + orchestration entrypoint)

All systems become **targets behind a unified connector interface**, not independently invoked endpoints.

---

# 1. CORE PRINCIPLE

### Canonical Rule

> All external interaction flows through one system: **JARVIS CONNECTOR LAYER (JCL)**

No direct:

* Supabase client calls outside SKADI
* GitHub API calls outside SKADI/GOD routing
* MCP tool execution outside ODIN classification

Everything is mediated.

---

# 2. ARCHITECTURE OVERVIEW

## New Layer: JCL (Jarvis Connector Layer)

```
USER / AGENT
    ↓
MCP ENTRYPOINT
    ↓
ODIN (intent classification)
    ↓
AEGIS (authorization gate)
    ↓
KRONOS (temporal + constraint validation)
    ↓
SKADI (execution runtime)
    ↓
JCL (connector abstraction layer)
    ↓
    ├── Supabase Adapter
    ├── GitHub Adapter
    └── MCP Tool Adapter
```

---

# 3. CONNECTOR ABSTRACTION MODEL

## 3.1 Unified Connector Interface

```ts
interface JCLRequest {
  trace_id: string;
  intent: "memory" | "event" | "decision" | "patch" | "github_commit" | "query";
  target: "supabase" | "github" | "mcp";
  operation: "read" | "write" | "update" | "delete";
  payload: any;
  metadata: {
    source: string;
    correlation_id: string;
    timestamp: string;
  };
}
```

---

## 3.2 Connector Response Contract

```ts
interface JCLResponse {
  trace_id: string;
  success: boolean;
  target: string;
  result?: any;
  error?: string;
  routed_by: "JCL";
}
```

---

# 4. CONNECTOR ADAPTERS

## 4.1 Supabase Adapter

### Responsibilities

* All writes to:

  * mnemos_memories
  * event_spine
  * execution_trace
  * decision_ledger
  * patch_proposals

### Rules

* MUST attach:

  * trace_id
  * correlation_id
* MUST pass through SKADI validation first

### Output

Normalized insert/update payload only (no SQL leakage upward)

---

## 4.2 GitHub Adapter

### Responsibilities

* Commits
* Branch creation
* PR generation
* Patch deployment sync

### Rules

* All commits require:

  * patch_id OR trace_id
  * KRONOS approval stage
* No direct git CLI calls outside adapter

### Output

```ts
{
  commit_hash,
  branch,
  status,
  linked_trace_id
}
```

---

## 4.3 MCP Adapter

### Responsibilities

* Tool invocation registry
* Tool routing normalization
* External agent tool calls (Claude/Codex/GPT)

### Rules

* Tools must be pre-registered in ODIN registry
* No dynamic tool invocation without classification

